# You do NOT need this file to try the template. With no key set, the build
# falls back to a shared read-only key against the demo conference, so
# `yarn install && yarn dev` works on a fresh clone.
#
# Set your own key once you point site.config.ts at your own event — create one
# for free at https://cloomba.com/me/developers. Pick the "Read Public"
# permission: it covers the public event content this template renders.
CLOOMBA_API_KEY=cloomba_sk_your_key_here

# Optional overrides — production defaults live in site.config.ts (api.*).
# Uncomment for local development against a dev Cloomba stack:
# CLOOMBA_API_URL=http://localhost:3070/public/v1
# CLOOMBA_BROWSER_API_URL=http://localhost:3070/v1
# CLOOMBA_EMBED_ORIGIN=http://localhost:3000

# Analytics — this repository commits no tracking id. Set one to enable Umami
# (the demo does this in its host's build environment).
# UMAMI_WEBSITE_ID=
